------------

© 2026 The MITRE Corporation. This work is reproduced and distributed with the permission of The MITRE Corporation.

The file `core/data/attack_lookup.json` holds 858 technique identifiers with
their ATT&CK technique names and tactic assignments, and the 15 Enterprise
tactics in matrix order. It was built from the Enterprise ATT&CK 19.1 STIX
distribution, published at https://attack.mitre.org. The same release is
recorded as `ATTACK_RELEASE` in `core/attack_mapping.py`, and its major number
is written into every ATT&CK Navigator layer that `meerkat export navigator`
produces.

AIT Alert Data Set
------------------

AIT Alert Data Set, by Max Landauer, Florian Skopik and Markus Wurzenberger,
AIT Austrian Institute of Technology.

  DOI     10.5281/zenodo.8263181
  Record  https://zenodo.org/records/8263181
  License Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC BY 4.0)
          https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

The full data set holds alerts from eight simulated company networks. One of the
eight, russellmitchell, is included here so that `meerkat demo` runs from a clone
with no download. The other seven stay in the Zenodo record and are needed to
reproduce the results table in README.md.

Copied unmodified from the data set:

  data/raw/russellmitchell_wazuh.json   45.3 MB, Wazuh and Suricata alerts (Git LFS)
  data/raw/russellmitchell_aminer.json   3.4 MB, AMiner alerts (Git LFS)
  data/labels.csv                        3.7 KB, the attack windows for all eight
                                         environments, byte-identical to the record

Derived from the data set:

  data/raw/inventory/*.json   converted from the environment configuration AIT
                              publishes alongside the alerts, into the inventory
                              format meerkat reads. Attacker-group assets were
                              left out. One address in the shaw environment was
                              added by hand and carries no groups.

  models/meerkat_bundle.skops a model, not alert data, but fitted on seven of the
                              eight environments, with a training profile that
                              summarises their alerts. Adapted material under the
                              same licence.

